    "chunk_text": "55 new hostel projects for 16,000 university students\n\nColombo, June 1 (Daily Mirror) - Fifty-five new hostel projects will be implemented for 16,000 students in state universities across the island, the Higher Education Division of the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education said.\n\nAccording to the Ministry, the projects are aimed at improving residential facilities for university students and will be carried out in three phases.\n\nThe initiative is expected to address accommodation shortages faced by undergraduates and enhance living conditions within state university premises.\n\nThe current progress of the hostel projects planned for each university is as follows:\n\nHostel types: 03 Model A hostels (400 students each) and 02 Model B hostels (200 students each).\n\nCurrent progress: Bids for the construction of one hostel were opened on April 30, 2026, and evaluations are currently underway to select the most suitable contractor.\n\nHostel types: 01 Model A hostel (400 students) and 01 Model B hostel (200 students).\n\nCurrent progress: Tenders for the construction of one hostel were opened on April 2, 2026, and the university is currently evaluating the proposals.\n\nHostel types: 04 Model A hostels (400 students each) and 03 Model B hostels (200 students each).\n\nCurrent progress: Tenders for the construction of one hostel were opened on May 20, 2026.\n\nHostel types: 04 Model A hostels (400 students each) and 02 Model B hostels (200 students each).\n\nCurrent progress: Tenders for the construction of one hostel were officially opened on May 21, 2026, and further action is underway.\n\nHostel types: 02 Model A hostels (400 students each) and 02 Model B hostels (200 students each).\n\nCurrent progress: Preparation of tender and legal documents for the construction of one hostel is currently underway.\n\nHostel types: 04 Model A hostels (400 students each) and 03 Model B hostels (200 students each)."
  },
