    "chunk_text": "CSE CEO Rajeeva Bandaranaike stated, \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s GSS+ bond market has evolved significantly within a relatively short period, transitioning from a nascent market towards a more structured and internationally recognised sustainable finance ecosystem. The continued collaboration between regulators, market institutions, development partners and initiatives such as the EU-funded Green Recovery Facility implemented by Expertise France has played an important role in strengthening market confidence, technical capacity and the pipeline of credible sustainable finance instruments.\u201d\n\nThis growing international recognition was further reinforced at the 2026 Environmental Finance Sustainable Debt Awards, where three Sri Lankan institutions, DFCC Bank, Bank of Ceylon and Commercial Bank of Ceylon, received international recognition for innovative GSS+ bond issuances, reflecting the market\u2019s growing credibility and international recognition."
