    "language": "en",
    "md5": "7b4ee1371a719877b50075be5692e49c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1897,
    "chunk_text": "hen experts say \"malware,\" they mean malicious software \u2014 any program intentionally designed to damage, disrupt, or gain unauthorised access to a computer, phone, or network. Think of it as a digital virus, but far more diverse.\n\nTrojans \u2013 Disguise themselves as legitimate apps (a game, a PDF, a banking tool) while hiding harmful functions.\n\nRansomware \u2013 Encrypts your files and demands payment to unlock them.\n\nSpyware \u2013 Sits silently, recording keystrokes, passwords, browsing habits, and even microphone or camera input.\n\nKeyloggers \u2013 A specific form of spyware that records every key you type, capturing passwords and messages.\n\nMany people mistakenly believe malware always causes obvious symptoms like a slow computer or pop-ups. In reality, sophisticated malware is designed to remain invisible. It may live on a device for months, quietly collecting banking credentials, contacts, photos, GPS location, behavioral patterns, and even voice recordings. The victim\u2019s phone works normally. Their bank balance appears intact. But behind the screen, data is being siphoned out daily.\n\nOne of the hidden realities of cybersecurity is that technology itself is not always the weakest point. Human psychology is.\n\nHackers increasingly exploit emotions rather than software vulnerabilities. Fear, urgency, greed, curiosity, loneliness, trust, and authority are weaponised to manipulate individuals into surrendering sensitive information voluntarily.\n\nFake banking alerts claiming your account will be suspended unless you click a link.\n\nDeepfake voice and video manipulation (AI-generated audio that sounds exactly like a relative).\n\n\u201cUnlike traditional hacking, social engineering bypasses firewalls and antivirus systems because the victim unknowingly opens the door themselves. This psychological dimension represents one of the most dangerous developments in the digital age.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-06-01-dailyftlk-f23a8e87",
    "num": "dailyftlk-f23a8e87",
    "date_str": "2026-06-01",
    "description": "The hidden side of cybersecurity",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/The-hidden-side-of-cybersecurity/4-792749",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
