    "chunk_text": "During the event, NCPC Sri Lanka Chief Executive Officer Samantha Kumarasena presented an overview of the upcoming Fourth International Conference on Resource Efficiency and Circular Economy, which will serve as a global platform for knowledge sharing, innovation, policy dialogue and collaboration among experts, industries, researchers and development organisations working towards a circular economy transition.\n\nAddressing the audience, Jayasundara commended the NCPC Sri Lanka for its continued leadership in promoting sustainable industrial development and encouraged greater participation from industries across the country in embracing resource-efficient and environmentally responsible practices.\n\nA key highlight of the event was the presentation of certification awards under two nationally recognised certification schemes operated by the NCPC Sri Lanka.\n\nThe launch event further acknowledged the invaluable support of its corporate partners, including Platinum Partner INSEE Ecocycle Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd and Exclusive Banking Partner Hatton National Bank PLC, whose commitment to sustainability continues to support the national environmental initiatives.\n\nNational Cleaner Production Awards 2026 and the Fourth International Conference on Resource Efficiency and Circular Economy are expected to attract wide participation from industries, policymakers, academics, development agencies and sustainability professionals, creating opportunities to showcase best practices, foster innovation and accelerate Sri Lanka\u2019s transition towards a resource-efficient and circular economy."
