    "chunk_size_bytes": 1762,
    "chunk_text": "SDF appoints Saliya Ranasinghe to board\n\nSarvodaya Development Finance PLC (SDF) has announced the appointment of Saliya J. Ranasinghe as a Non-Executive, Non-Independent Director of the company, with effect from June 1, 2026.\n\nRanasinghe brings to the board more than 35 years of experience across financial inclusion, banking, microfinance, green finance, renewable energy and the development sector.\n\nHis career spans a wide range of regional and international assignments, with particular emphasis on strengthening inclusive financial systems and supporting development finance initiatives across the Asia-Pacific markets.\n\nHe previously served as Financial Inclusion Advisor to the Bank of Papua New Guinea\u2019s Centre for Excellence in Financial Inclusion (CEFI) and has also worked as a financial product development specialist for microfinance and employment-related projects. His leadership experience includes serving as Team Leader for the Microfinance Expansion Project and as Executive Director of CEFI.\n\nRanasinghe has worked extensively with leading bilateral and multilateral agencies, including the World Bank, IFC, Asian Development Bank, UNCDF, ODA UK and Dutch Development Corporation.\n\nHis professional engagements have covered project design, consultancy, implementation leadership and development project management, with a strong focus on financial inclusion, microfinance and sustainable economic development.\n\nHe is a Fellow Member of the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants, UK, a Member of the Chartered Global Management Accountant, USA and a Fellow Member of the Society of Certified Management Accountants of Sri Lanka. He is also an Honorary Fellow of the Institute of Banking and Business Management in Papua New Guinea."
