    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bb063564d8696214e383ffc78c0aada0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1456,
    "chunk_text": "Central to this domestic dominance is a targeted focus on novel therapies for non-communicable diseases, notably offering affordable alternatives such as its flagship diabetes medication, EmpaMor, which alone generated estimated annual savings of over Rs. 300 million for local patients.\n\nIn late March 2026, National Medicines Regulatory Authority (NMRA) Chairman Specialist Dr. Ananda Wijewickrama confirmed that pharmaceutical companies formally wrote to Health Ministry Secretary Specialist Dr. Anil Jasinghe, requesting a price hike of at least 7 percent for 60 price-controlled medicines. Manufacturers argue that surging global production costs, a weakening local currency, and elevated shipping and insurance charges linked to the ongoing Middle East conflict have made current price points unsustainable.\n\nSecuring the globally recognised EU-GMP certification will serve as a critical inflection point for the manufacturer, unlocking immediate access to highly regulated international markets and mitigating these local macroeconomic vulnerabilities. This evolution aligns with a broader corporate restructuring that began when Hemas Holdings took Morison Limited, delisting the firm from the Colombo Stock Exchange in 2020. The delisting provided the strategic freedom to absorb heavy, long-term capital expenditures - such as the massive investment in the Homagama plant - without the immediate pressures of quarterly public market expectations."
  },
