    "chunk_size_bytes": 1158,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka tourist arrivals top one million mark\n\nColombo, June 3 (Daily MIrror) - Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry has surpassed the one-million visitor mark, recording 1,022,022 tourist arrivals during the first five months of 2026, according to the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA).\n\nThe SLTDA said 145,745 tourists arrived in the country between May 1 and May 31 alone, reflecting the sector\u2019s continued growth and rising global confidence in Sri Lanka as a travel destination.\n\nIndia remained the leading source market during May, contributing 60,342 visitors. Other top-performing markets during the month included the United Kingdom, China, Germany and Australia.\n\nMeanwhile, from January 1 to May 31, India maintained its position as Sri Lanka\u2019s largest tourist source market with 250,260 arrivals.\n\nThe United Kingdom, Russian Federation, China and Germany also ranked among the top five source markets during the same period.\n\nThe latest figures point to a positive trend for Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry, which continues to play a key role in supporting the country\u2019s economic recovery and generating foreign exchange earnings."
