    "chunk_text": "DMASL and LIA continue collaboration to elevate Sri Lankan creativity on global stage\n\nThe Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka (DMASL) announced the continuation of its partnership with the London International Awards (LIA), reaffirming a shared commitment to nurturing creative excellence, fostering global exposure, and creating meaningful opportunities for Sri Lanka\u2019s advertising, marketing, and creative community.\n\nFollowing a successful collaboration in 2025, the renewed partnership aims to further strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s presence within the global creative landscape while providing local professionals with greater access to international recognition, learning opportunities, and industry-leading networks.\n\nEstablished in 1986, the London International Awards is one of the world\u2019s most respected award platforms, and is one of only five global shows included in the WARC Creative 100, celebrating excellence across advertising, design, digital, production, technology, creativity, and branded communications. Known for its commitment to recognising outstanding creative work, LIA continues to serve as a benchmark for excellence within the global industry.\n\nAs part of the continued partnership, Sri Lankan agencies, brands, creators, and independent professionals will once again gain access to opportunities that extend beyond awards and recognition, helping bridge local talent with the international creative community. DMASL also encourages agencies, marketing teams, brands, creators, and independent professionals across Sri Lanka to actively submit their best work for international award consideration. Participating in globally recognised platforms such as LIA not only provides an opportunity for recognition but also helps benchmark local work against international standards, showcase Sri Lankan creativity to the world, and inspire the industry to continue raising the bar for excellence."
  },
