    "md5": "77e368120af201da87375e9679fa07fe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "Capital Trust Properties extends partnership with John Keells Properties\n\nCapital Trust Properties (CTP) has renewed its partnership with John Keells Properties to market its residential developments, including Cinnamon Life, TRI-ZEN, Viman and Vauxhall DSTRCT.\n\nThe renewed partnership marks another milestone in Capital Trust Properties\u2019 long-standing role in Sri Lanka\u2019s real estate sector, where the company has built a reputation for providing end-to-end property transaction and advisory solutions for leading developers, investors and homeowners.\n\nFounded in 2010, Capital Trust Properties has grown into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading property transaction companies, offering a comprehensive suite of services including legal coordination, valuations, interior solutions, transaction advisory, development advisory and coordination, mortgage recommendations, rental advisory, furnishing support and developer due diligence.\n\nThe company\u2019s partnership approach is built on selectivity, credibility and long-term value creation. Capital Trust Properties evaluates developers and developments based on ethical standards, financial credibility, transparency and due diligence, ensuring that clients and investors are guided towards projects that meet strong governance and market standards.\n\nCommenting on the renewed partnership, Capital Trust Properties Chairperson, CEO and Founder, Minoli Wickramasinghe said, \u201cOur partnership with John Keells Properties reflects the standards we have consistently upheld as a company, built on credibility, professionalism, transparency and ethical business conduct. We do not view real estate purely as a transaction. Our role is to guide clients with the right information, support developers with structured advisory solutions, and help create long-term value for all stakeholders. Renewing this partnership is an important step in continuing that commitment with one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most respected developers.\u201d"
  },
