    "chunk_text": "Principal CSE indices do a dip; regional markets too finish low\n\nThe CSE closed down yesterday with the benchmark All Share Price Index moving down 0.75 percent.\n\nThe ASPI was down 166.55 points at 22,011.10, while the more liquid S&P SL20 was down 0.54 percent, or 32.82 points, at 6,097.83.\n\nPositive contributors to the ASPI were JKH (up 0.50 percent at Rs 20.10 ), Lion Brewery Ceylon (up 2.85 percent at Rs 1,849.00 ), and Seylan Developments (up 11.11 percent at Rs 1.00 ).\n\nDialog Axiata (down 2.51 percent at Rs 42.80 ), Sampath Bank (down 0.88 percent at Rs 140.75 ), Ceylon Beverage Holdings (down 6.28 percent at Rs 2,750.75 ), and Ceylon Cold Stores (down 3.22 percent at Rs 135.25) were top negative contributors.\n\nMarket turnover was Rs 2.05 billion . It is said that Consumer Durables & Apparels led the turnover with Rs 413.9 million .\n\nAnalysts noted that regional markets also finished lower, with Hong Kong\u2019s Hang Seng index down 1.56 percent at 25,633.21 and India\u2019s Nifty 50 dropping 0.33 percent to 23,405.60.\n\nMeanwhile, Maharaja Foods announced the opening of its newest retail outlet, \u201cMaharaja Super \u2013 SPAR Savemore\u201d in Kotahena on June 1.\n\nYesterday the rupee was quoted at Rs 333.00/335.50 to the US dollar in the spot market on, weaker from Rs 332.00/333.50 the previous day, dealers said, while bond yields were broadly steady.\n\nThe telegraphic transfer rate for Sri Lanka\u2019s rupee against the US dollar was 328.50 buying, 337.50 selling.\n\nUSD 50 mn battery storage investment expected to power SL\u2019s renewable energy push\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
