    "chunk_text": "From December 2025 onwards, revenue from the business was recorded under Volt Industrial Company Ltd., a fully owned subsidiary of JAT Holdings. The business is also laying the foundation for its own charger network with recurring revenue potential, with 17 chargers already installed.\n\nCEO Nishal Ferdinando said: \u201cFY25/26 demonstrates the value of the strategic choices we have made over the past several years. We have continued to strengthen the core coatings business, improve manufacturing control, manage finance costs more effectively, and invest in platforms that expand JAT\u2019s long-term growth potential. The improvement in gross margin is particularly important because it reflects not only revenue growth, but better-quality growth. As we move forward, our focus is on scaling these platforms with discipline, while ensuring that JAT remains competitive and positioned for sustained value creation.\u201d\n\nManaging Director Aelian Gunawardene added: \u201cJAT\u2019s growth has always been built on the belief that we must develop capability ahead of opportunity. FY25/26 was an important year in that journey, as we strengthened our manufacturing base, expanded our international presence, and continued to invest in the businesses and systems that will give JAT greater depth, agility and relevance across markets. What we are building is not only a stronger company for today, but a Sri Lankan multinational grounded in technical superiority, customer service and innovation, with the reach and resilience to compete across markets over the long term.\u201d"
